{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:33251544 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:33251544 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"33251544","source":"MED","pmid":"33251544","doi":"10.1093/jaoacint/qsaa084","title":"Inter-Laboratory Validation of 4-(Dimethylamino) Cinnamaldehyde (DMAC) Assay Using Cranberry Proanthocyanidin Standard for Quantification of Soluble Proanthocyanidins in Cranberry Foods and Dietary Supplements, First Action Official MethodSM: 2019.06.","authorString":"Birmingham AD, Esquivel-Alvarado D, Maranan M, Krueger CG, Reed JD.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Birmingham AD","lastName":"Birmingham","firstName":"Andrew D","initials":"AD","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complete Phytochemical Solutions, LLC, 275 Rodney Road, Cambridge, WI 53523, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Esquivel-Alvarado D","lastName":"Esquivel-Alvarado","firstName":"Daniel","initials":"D","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3557-2562"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"University of Wisconsin-Madison, Department of Animal Sciences, Reed Research Group, 1675 Observatory Drive, Madison, WI 53706, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Maranan M","lastName":"Maranan","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complete Phytochemical Solutions, LLC, 275 Rodney Road, Cambridge, WI 53523, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Krueger CG","lastName":"Krueger","firstName":"Christian G","initials":"CG","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4242-9596"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complete Phytochemical Solutions, LLC, 275 Rodney Road, Cambridge, WI 53523, USA."},{"affiliation":"University of Wisconsin-Madison, Department of Animal Sciences, Reed Research Group, 1675 Observatory Drive, Madison, WI 53706, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Reed JD","lastName":"Reed","firstName":"Jess D","initials":"JD","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Complete Phytochemical Solutions, LLC, 275 Rodney Road, Cambridge, WI 53523, USA."},{"affiliation":"University of Wisconsin-Madison, Department of Animal Sciences, Reed Research Group, 1675 Observatory Drive, Madison, WI 53706, USA."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3557-2562"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4242-9596"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"104","journalIssueId":3136999,"dateOfPublication":"2021 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2021,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J AOAC Int","title":"Journal of AOAC International","essn":"1944-7922","issn":"1060-3271","isoabbreviation":"J AOAC Int","nlmid":"9215446"},"printPublicationDate":"2021-03-01"},"pubYear":"2021","pageInfo":"216-222","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Proanthocyanidins (PAC) are oligomers and polymers of flavan-3-ols with putative health benefits. PAC are prevalent in a wide variety of natural products and dietary supplements.<h4>Objective</h4>An inter-laboratory study was conducted to validate the 4-(dimethylamino)cinnamaldehyde (DMAC) colorimetric assay using a 96-well plate spectrophotometer for the accurate quantification of PAC in cranberry products and to evaluate the comparison of the procyanidin A2 (ProA2) dimer and cranberry PAC (c-PAC) reference standards.<h4>Methods</h4>Four test materials analyzed in this study included cranberry fiber powder, cranberry extract powder, concentrated cranberry juice, and a solution of cranberry PAC (30%, w/v). The samples were homogenized, extracted, sonicated, centrifuged, and analyzed using a 96-well plate spectrophotometer.<h4>Results</h4>Linearity for both the ProA2 and c-PAC standards was determined from 4.053 to 50.666 µg/mL and from 13.520 to 135.95 µg/mL, respectively. The relative standard deviation of repeatability (RSDr) values for the four materials analyzed, using both ProA2 and c-PAC standards, met the Standard Method Performance Requirements (SMPR®). Inter-laboratory precision using Horwitz ratio (HorRat) values for the four materials analyzed, using both ProA2 and c-PAC standards, satisfies the acceptance range in Appendix K of the Official Methods of Analysis (2003): Guidelines for Dietary Supplements and Botanicals. The limit of quantification (LOQ) was estimated to be 3.16 µg/mL.<h4>Conclusions</h4>The results produced from this study demonstrate the utility of the c-PAC standard over the ProA2 standard and the advantages of using a 96-well plate spectrophotometer for the accurate quantification of PAC.<h4>Highlights</h4>The use of a 96-well plate reader and c-PAC reference standard in the DMAC method improves accuracy and percision for quantification of soluble proanthocyanidins in cranberry foods and dietary supplements.","affiliation":"Complete Phytochemical Solutions, LLC, 275 Rodney Road, Cambridge, WI 53523, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Council for Scientific and Technology Research","grantId":"PED-056-2015-I","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Innovation and Human Capital Program for Competitiveness","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Ministry of Science, Technology and Telecommunications","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Vaccinium macrocarpon"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Acrolein","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AA","qualifierName":"analogs & derivatives"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Proanthocyanidins"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Plant Extracts"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Dietary Supplements"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Laboratories"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"proanthocyanidin","registryNumber":"18206-61-6"},{"name":"Plant Extracts","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Proanthocyanidins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Acrolein","registryNumber":"7864XYD3JJ"},{"name":"cinnamaldehyde","registryNumber":"SR60A3XG0F"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jaoacint/qsaa084"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":11,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2021-06-25","dateOfCreation":"2020-11-30","dateOfRevision":"2021-07-02","firstPublicationDate":"2021-03-01","firstIndexDate":"2020-12-01","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}